95731354,-0.0511317104101181,-0.23262368142604828,-1.3095563650131226,-0.10328495502471924,-0.0004847066884394735,-7.915183232398704e-05,-0.23551954329013824,-0.8343791365623474,-0.0015572099946439266,-0.012053156271576881,-3.635817120084539e-05,-0.057648997753858566,-0.07608859241008759,-0.00010501786891836673,-0.00047302976599894464,-0.2388969212770462,-0.0004553949984256178,-8.583032467868179e-06,-0.13103337585926056,-0.0014132998185232282,-0.08517882227897644,-0.47304338216781616,-1.5006314516067505,-0.00011729506513802335,-0.0028388698119670153,-0.18054310977458954,-0.025400035083293915,0.0,-2.3841855067985307e-07,-4.768370445162873e-07,-1.1920928244535389e-07,-9.536738616588991e-07,-0.0002244459028588608,-9.536738616588991e-07,-1.1920928244535389e-07,-2.4676019165781327e-05,-2.3841855067985307e-07,-3.576278118089249e-07,-7.986990567587782e-06,-0.0073643880896270275,-5.602679812000133e-05,-4.3748852476710454e-05,-0.00026174934464506805,-0.060655925422906876,-5.960446742392378e-06,-1.0371154530730564e-05,-2.658331868587993e-05,-0.00010799778101500124,-4.887569048150908e-06,-1.2874520507466514e-05,-0.7323480248451233,-0.004791682120412588,-0.0011360150529071689,-0.13086417317390442,-0.0001333863037871197,-4.31528314948082e-05,-0.02809930592775345,0.0,-0.009614944458007812,-3.576278118089249e-07,-1.1920928244535389e-07,0.0,-0.0026689881924539804,-0.0009583409409970045,-0.0002728328399825841,-8.344646857949556e-07,0.0,-2.753696753643453e-05,-1.0609570381348021e-05],"request":{"active_prefix":"","input_ids":[151644,8948,198,2610,525,1207,16948,11,3465,553,54364,14817,13,1446,525,264,10950,17847,13,151645,198,151644,872,198,50,3948,279,3491,3019,553,3019,13,20678,697,1590,4226,304,1124,79075,90,1112,92,382,2132,374,2661,429,57960,839,15159,21,92,64,488,1124,839,15159,21,92,65,488,1124,839,15159,21,92,66,284,220,21,54876,1380,400,64,54876,400,65,54876,323,400,66,3,525,6785,25780,429,1352,458,7703,52484,8500,323,400,65,481,264,3,374,279,9334,315,458,7546,13,7379,400,64,488,293,488,272,12947,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nIt is given that $\\log_{6}a + \\log_{6}b + \\log_{6}c = 6$, where $a$, $b$, and $c$ are positive integers that form an increasing geometric sequence and $b - a$ is the square of an integer. Find $a + b + c$.","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"9392a1687ef438ff2a997e95f0840ccd7d60dec64f75a253a125c5dfcdd6fbe7"},"seconds":70.9013614654541,"seed":235135719192237848,"stop":"eos","text":"Given that \\(\\log_{6}a + \\log_{6}b + \\log_{6}c = 6\\), we can combine the logarithms using the property of logarithms \\(\\log_b(xy) = \\log_b x + \\log_b y\\). Hence,\n\n\\[\n\\log_{6} (abc) = 6\n\\]\n\nThis implies:\n\n\\[\nabc = 6^6\n\\]\n\nSince \\(6 = 2 \\times 3\\), we have:\n\n\\[\n6^6 = (2 \\times 3)^6 = 2^6 \\times 3^6\n\\]\n\nThus,\n\n\\[\nabc = 2^6 \\times 3^6\n\\]\n\nGiven that \\(a\\), \\(b\\), and \\(c\\) form an increasing geometric sequence, we can write \\(a\\), \\(b\\), and \\(c\\) as \\(a\\), \\(ar\\), and \\(ar^2\\), where \\(r\\) is the common ratio. Therefore,\n\n\\[\nabc = a \\cdot ar \\cdot ar^2 = a^3 r^3 = (ar)^3\n\\]\n\nSubstituting \\(abc = 2^6 \\times 3^6\\):\n\n\\[\n(ar)^3 = 2^6 \\times 3^6\n\\]\n\nTaking the cube root of both sides:\n\n\\[\nar = 2^2 \\times 3^2 = 4 \\times 9 = 36\n\\]\n\nThus, \\(ar = 36\\). Given that \\(a\\), \\(b\\), and \\(c\\) are in geometric sequence, we have \\(b = ar = 36\\).\n\nNow, we need to find \\(a\\) and \\(c\\). Since \\(ar = 36\\), we have:\n\n\\[\na \\cdot r = 36 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad c = ar^2\n\\]\n\nSince \\(b - a\\) is the square of an integer, we have:\n\n\\[\nb - a = 36 - a = k^2 \\quad \\text{for some integer } k\n\\]\n\nWe also know that \\(a\\) and \\(r\\) must be integers, and \\(a\\) and \\(r\\) should be factors of 36. Let’s check the possible pairs \\((a, r)\\):\n\n1. \\(a = 4\\), \\(r = 9\\):\n   \\[\n   b = 36, \\quad c = 36 \\times 9 = 324\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   b - a = 36 - 4 = 32 \\quad \\text{(not a perfect square)}\n   \\]\n\n2. \\(a = 9\\), \\(r = 4\\):\n   \\[\n   b = 36, \\quad c = 36 \\times 4 = 144\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   b - a = 36 - 9 = 27 \\quad \\text{(not a perfect square)}\n   \\]\n\n3. \\(a = 12\\), \\(r = 3\\):\n   \\[\n   b = 36, \\quad c = 36 \\times 3 = 108\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   b - a = 36 - 12 = 24 \\quad \\text{(not a perfect square)}\n   \\]\n\n4. \\(a = 18\\), \\(r = 2\\):\n   \\[\n   b = 36, \\quad c = 36 \\times 2 = 72\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   b - a = 36 - 18 = 18 \\quad \\text{(not a perfect square)}\n   \\]\n\n5. \\(a = 24\\), \\(r = \\frac{3}{2}\\):\n   \\[\n   \\text{Not integers, discard}\n   \\]\n\n6. \\(a = 36\\), \\(r = 1\\):\n   \\[\n   \\text{Not increasing geometric sequence, discard}\n   \\]\n\n7. \\(a = 6\\), \\(r = 6\\):\n   \\[\n   b = 36, \\quad c = 36 \\times 6 = 216\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   b - a = 36 - 6 = 30 \\quad \\text{(not a perfect square)}\n   \\]\n\n8. \\(a = 2\\), \\(r = 18\\):\n   \\[\n   b = 36, \\quad c = 36 \\times 18 = 648\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   b - a = 36 - 2 = 34 \\quad \\text{(not a perfect square)}\n   \\]\n\nFinally, we find:\n\n\\[\na = 6, r = 6 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad b = 36, c = 216\n\\]\n\nThus,\n\n\\[\na + b + c = 6 + 36 + 216 = 258\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the final answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{258}\n\\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{258}","correct":false,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
